{"type":"message","id":"fd68a305","parentId":"621b431d","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:00:59.243Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll create the osint-search-multi skill. This will query multiple search engines including Brave and potentially Google via scraping. I'll create a modular search system that can use Brave Search API and also implement basic fallbacks.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_991b1938501b43de9c76683e","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# osint-search-multi - Multi-Engine Search\n\n## Description\nQuery multiple search engines simultaneously for comprehensive OSINT research. Currently supports Brave Search API with extensible architecture for adding other engines (Google via scraping, Bing, DuckDuckGo, etc.).\n\n## Usage\n```\nosint-search-multi <query> [options]\n```\n\n## Parameters\n- `query` (required): Search query string\n- `--engines, -e` (optional): Comma-separated list of engines to query (default: 'brave')\n- `--count, -n` (optional): Number of results per engine (default: 10, max: 50)\n- `--output, -o` (optional): Output file path\n- `--format, -f` (optional): Output format: 'json', 'csv', 'text' (default: 'text')\n- `--country, -c` (optional): Country code for localized results (e.g., US, GB, IN, DE)\n- `--language, -l` (optional): Language code (e.g., en, es, fr, de)\n- `--safeSearch, -s` (optional): Enable SafeSearch filtering (default: false)\n- `--freshness, -F` (optional): Time filter: 'pd' (day), 'pw' (week), 'pm' (month), 'py' (year)\n- `--timeout, -t` (optional): Overall timeout in ms (default: 30000)\n\n## Examples\n\n**Basic Brave search:**\n```\nosint-search-multi \"openclaw framework\"\n```\n\n**Multi-engine search (current: brave only, extensible):**\n```\nosint-search-multi \"cybersecurity trends\" --engines brave --count 20\n```\n\n**Localized search:**\n```\nosint-search-multi \"osint tools\" --country US --language en\n```\n\n**Recent results only:**\n```\nosint-search-multi \"data breach 2024\" --freshness pw\n```\n\n## Output\nResults array contains:\n- `engine`: Source engine name\n- `title`: Result title\n- `url`: Result URL\n- `snippet`: Description/context snippet\n- `publishedAt`: Publication date (if available)\n- `source`: Source domain\n- `type`: Result type (news, web, video, etc.)\n\n## Capabilities\n- ✅ Brave Search API integration\n- ✅ Country and language localization\n- ✅ SafeSearch filtering\n- ✅ Freshness/time-based filtering\n- ✅ Concurrent multi-engine queries\n- ✅ Configurable result limits\n- ✅ CSV/JSON/text output formats\n- ✅ Error handling with partial result aggregation\n- ✅ Extensible engine architecture\n\n## Limitations\n- Brave API has rate limits (free tier: ~50 requests/day)\n- Google scraping not implemented (legal/ToS concerns)\n- No authentication for premium search APIs\n- Some engines may block automated queries\n- Result deduplication not performed across engines\n- Country/language filters depend on API support\n\n## Notes\n- Brave Search provides good results with generous free tier\n- For production use, consider API keys for higher limits\n- Extensible design allows adding new engines via Engine subclasses\n- Always respect robots.txt and Terms of Service\n- Consider caching results for repeated queries\n- Use --timeout to prevent hanging on slow engines\n\n## Extending\nTo add new search engines, create a class extending SearchEngine with:\n- `name`: Engine identifier\n- `search(query, options)`: Returns Promise<{results, total}> \n- Implement results in standard format","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-osint\\skills\\osint-search-multi\\SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":25714,"output":919,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26633,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419644359}}
{"type":"message","id":"4b6c7c3e","parentId":"fd68a305","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:00:59.302Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_991b1938501b43de9c76683e","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 2970 bytes to D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-osint\\skills\\osint-search-multi\\SKILL.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771419659296}}
{"type":"message","id":"6705dbfa","parentId":"4b6c7c3e","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:01:18.987Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me create the implementation for osint-search-multi. I'll create a modular system with a base SearchEngine class and specific implementations for Brave and potential fallbacks.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8039400ca36d40dc8ec7846a","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n\nimport axios from 'axios';\nimport { pipeline } from 'stream/promises';\nimport { createWriteStream } from 'fs';\nimport { stringify } from 'csv-stringify/sync';\n\n/**\n * OSINT Multi-Engine Search - Query multiple search engines\n */\n\nclass SearchEngine {\n  constructor(name) {\n    this.name = name;\n  }\n\n  async search(query, options) {\n    throw new Error('Subclasses must implement search()');\n  }\n\n  normalizeResults(rawResults) {\n    return rawResults.map(r => ({\n      engine: this.name,\n      title: r.title || '',\n      url: r.url || '',\n      snippet: r.snippet || r.description || '',\n      publishedAt: r.publishedAt || r.date || null,\n      source: r.source || this.extractDomain(r.url),\n      type: r.type || 'web'\n    }));\n  }\n\n  extractDomain(url) {\n    try {\n      return new URL(url).hostname;\n    } catch (e) {\n      return '';\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nclass BraveSearchEngine extends SearchEngine {\n  constructor(apiKey = null) {\n    super('brave');\n    this.apiKey = apiKey || process.env.BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY;\n    this.baseUrl = 'https://api.search.brave.com/res/v1/web/search';\n  }\n\n  async search(query, options = {}) {\n    const params = {\n      q: query,\n      count: options.count || 10,\n      ...(options.country && { country: options.country }),\n      ...(options.language && { search_lang: options.language }),\n      ...(options.safeSearch && { safesearch: 'strict' }),\n      ...(options.freshness && { freshness: options.freshness })\n    };\n\n    const headers = {\n      'Accept': 'application/json'\n    };\n\n    if (this.apiKey) {\n      headers['X-Subscription-Token'] = this.apiKey;\n    } else {\n      // Use free endpoint (rate-limited)\n      console.warn('[OSINT] Brave Search API key not set. Using free tier with limited results.');\n    }\n\n    try {\n      const response = await axios.get(this.baseUrl, {\n        params,\n        headers,\n        timeout: options.timeout || 30000\n      });\n\n      const results = response.data.web?.results || response.data.results || [];\n      return {\n        total: response.data.web?.total_results || results.length,\n        results: this.normalizeResults(results)\n      };\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(`[OSINT] Brave search error:`, error.message);\n      throw error;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Placeholder for future engines\nclass GoogleSearchEngine extends SearchEngine {\n  constructor(apiKey = null, cseId = null) {\n    super('google');\n    this.apiKey = apiKey;\n    this.cseId = cseId;\n    this.baseUrl = 'https://www.googleapis.com/customsearch/v1';\n  }\n\n  async search(query, options = {}) {\n    // Not implemented - Google Custom Search API requires setup\n    console.warn('[OSINT] Google search not implemented. Requires Custom Search API setup.');\n    return { total: 0, results: [] };\n  }\n}\n\nclass DuckDuckGoSearchEngine extends SearchEngine {\n  constructor() {\n    super('duckduckgo');\n    this.baseUrl = 'https://api.duckduckgo.com/';\n  }\n\n  async search(query, options = {}) {\n    // DuckDuckGo Instant Answer API (limited)\n    console.warn('[OSINT] DuckDuckGo search not fully implemented. Limited to instant answers.');\n    return { total: 0, results: [] };\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Main OSINT Search Multi Engine\n */\nclass OSINTSearchMulti {\n  constructor(options = {}) {\n    this.options = {\n      engines: ['brave'],\n      count: 10,\n      output: null,\n      format: 'text',\n      country: null,\n      language: null,\n      safeSearch: false,\n      freshness: null,\n      timeout: 30000,\n      ...options\n    };\n\n    this.engines = this.initEngines();\n  }\n\n  initEngines() {\n    const instances = [];\n    \n    for (const engineName of this.options.engines) {\n      switch (engineName.toLowerCase()) {\n        case 'brave':\n          instances.push(new BraveSearchEngine());\n          break;\n        case 'google':\n          instances.push(new GoogleSearchEngine());\n          break;\n        case 'duckduckgo':\n          instances.push(new DuckDuckGoSearchEngine());\n          break;\n        default:\n          console.warn(`[OSINT] Unknown engine: ${engineName}. Skipping.`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    return instances;\n  }\n\n  async search(query) {\n    console.log(`[OSINT] Multi-engine search: \"${query}\"`);\n    console.log(`[OSINT] Engines: ${this.engines.map(e => e.name).join(', ')}`);\n\n    const allResults = [];\n    const errors = [];\n\n    // Execute searches in parallel\n    const promises = this.engines.map(async (engine, index) => {\n      try {\n        console.log(`[OSINT] Querying ${engine.name}...`);\n        const result = await engine.search(query, {\n          count: this.options.count,\n          country: this.options.country,\n          language: this.options.language,\n          safeSearch: this.options.safeSearch,\n          freshness: this.options.freshness,\n          timeout: this.options.timeout\n        });\n\n        allResults.push({\n          engine: engine.name,\n          total: result.total,\n          results: result.results\n        });\n\n        console.log(`[OSINT] ${engine.name}: ${result.results.length} results`);\n      } catch (error) {\n        errors.push({ engine: engine.name, error: error.message });\n        console.error(`[OSINT] ${engine.name} failed:`, error.message);\n      }\n    });\n\n    await Promise.allSettled(promises);\n\n    if (errors.length > 0) {\n      console.warn(`[OSINT] ${errors.length} engine(s) failed. Results may be incomplete.`);\n    }\n\n    const finalResults = {\n      query,\n      enginesQueried: this.engines.map(e => e.name),\n      enginesSucceeded: allResults.map(r => r.engine),\n      totalResults: allResults.reduce((sum, r) => sum + r.results.length, 0),\n      results: allResults.flatMap(r => r.results),\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n      errors: errors\n    };\n\n    if (this.options.output) {\n      await this.saveResults(finalResults);\n    }\n\n    return finalResults;\n  }\n\n  async saveResults(results) {\n    let content;\n    \n    if (this.options.format === 'json') {\n      content = JSON.stringify(results, null, 2);\n    } else if (this.options.format === 'csv') {\n      content = this.toCSV(results);\n    } else {\n      content = this.formatText(results);\n    }\n\n    await require('fs').promises.writeFile(this.options.output, content, 'utf8');\n    console.log(`[OSINT] Results saved to ${this.options.output} (${results.results.length} total)`);\n  }\n\n  toCSV(results) {\n    const rows = [\n      ['engine', 'title', 'url', 'snippet', 'publishedAt', 'source', 'type']\n    ];\n\n    for (const result of results.results) {\n      rows.push([\n        result.engine,\n        this.escapeCSV(result.title),\n        result.url,\n        this.escapeCSV(result.snippet),\n        result.publishedAt || '',\n        result.source,\n        result.type\n      ]);\n    }\n\n    return stringify(rows, { header: false });\n  }\n\n  escapeCSV(str) {\n    if (str.includes(',') || str.includes('\"') || str.includes('\\n')) {\n      return `\"${str.replace(/\"/g, '\"\"')}\"`;\n    }\n    return str;\n  }\n\n  formatText(results) {\n    const lines = [];\n    lines.push('===============================================');\n    lines.push('           MULTI-ENGINE SEARCH REPORT         ');\n    lines.push('===============================================\\n');\n    \n    lines.push(`Query: \"${results.query}\"`);\n    lines.push(`Engines: ${results.enginesQueried.join(', ')}`);\n    lines.push(`Total Results: ${results.totalResults}`);\n    lines.push(`Timestamp: ${results.timestamp}\\n`);\n\n    for (const result of results.results.slice(0, 50)) { // Limit display\n      lines.push(`[${result.engine}] ${result.title}`);\n      lines.push(`  URL: ${result.url}`);\n      lines.push(`  Source: ${result.source}`);\n      if (result.snippet) {\n        lines.push(`  ${result.snippet.substring(0, 150)}...`);\n      }\n      lines.push('');\n    }\n\n    if (results.results.length > 50) {\n      lines.push(`... and ${results.results.length - 50} more results (see output file)`);\n    }\n\n    if (results.errors.length > 0) {\n      lines.push('\\nErrors:');\n      for (const err of results.errors) {\n        lines.push(`  ${err.engine}: ${err.error}`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    return lines.join('\\n');\n  }\n}\n\n// CLI Interface\nif (import.meta.url === `file://${process.argv[1]}`) {\n  const args = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\n  \n  const search = new OSINTSearchMulti(args.options);\n  \n  search.search(args.query)\n    .then(results => process.exit(0))\n    .catch(error => {\n      console.error('[OSINT] Search failed:', error.message);\n      process.exit(1);\n    });\n}\n\nfunction parseArgs(args) {\n  const result = { query: null, options: {} };\n  \n  for (let i = 0; i < args.length; i++) {\n    const arg = args[i];\n    \n    if (!arg.startsWith('-') && !result.query) {\n      result.query = arg;\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    switch (arg) {\n      case '--engines':\n      case '-e':\n        result.options.engines = args[++i].split(',');\n        break;\n      case '--count':\n      case '-n':\n        result.options.count = parseInt(args[++i]);\n        break;\n      case '--output':\n      case '-o':\n        result.options.output = args[++i];\n        break;\n      case '--format':\n      case '-f':\n        result.options.format = args[++i];\n        break;\n      case '--country':\n      case '-c':\n        result.options.country = args[++i];\n        break;\n      case '--language':\n      case '-l':\n        result.options.language = args[++i];\n        break;\n      case '--safeSearch':\n      case '-s':\n        result.options.safeSearch = true;\n        break;\n      case '--freshness':\n      case '-F':\n        result.options.freshness = args[++i];\n        break;\n      case '--timeout':\n      case '-t':\n        result.options.timeout = parseInt(args[++i]);\n        break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (!result.query) {\n    console.error('Usage: osint-search-multi <query> [options]');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n\nexport default OSINTSearchMulti;","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-osint\\skills\\osint-search-multi\\osint-search-multi.js"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":26624,"output":2600,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29224,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419659302}}
